File: rust/lichen-schc/src/fragment.rs
Lines: 746-752

FragmentReceiver takes a pre-allocated storage buffer:

  pub fn new(storage: &mut [u8]) -> Result<Self, FragmentError> {
      let limit = storage.len().min(MAX_PACKET_SIZE);

This design prevents memory exhaustion attacks where an attacker sends fragments claiming arbitrarily large packet sizes. The receiver cannot be tricked into allocating beyond the pre-provided buffer.
